{{also|ȝwo}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|zwō}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*twaōz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*twōz}} (see {{m|gem-pro|*twai}}), from {{der|de|ine-pro|*dwóh₁}}. ''Zwo'' was originally feminine (see {{m|de|zween}}), but is now used as a variant of {{m|de|zwei}} without gender distinction. Compare, however, {{cog|lb|zwou}}, which is still a feminine form of {{m|lb|zwéin}}. The same is true of some German dialects, e.g. in Switzerland. More at ''[[two]]''.

